            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "s"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/systems_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 306,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "In multi-host use-case the redfish 'system' would correspond to a \n`xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Decorator.ManagedHost`, right?\n\nAt least this is how i saw it here https://github.com/openbmc/bmcweb/blob/50d9f38ab85cef8b09c5968d7df3be948cf50d2f/redfish-core/include/utils/systems_utils.hpp#L108"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/systems_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 306,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Could we add xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Decorator.ManagedHost  to this interfaces list? Does that solve the problem?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/systems_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 306,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "I assume the set of redfish resources which should? support `LocationIndicatorActive` property (on a given system) would be a (non-strict? (depending on system)) superset of the systems collection, right?\n\nSystems collection is created via managed host interface in multi-host systems.\n\nTL;DR, yes, i guess that should help."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/systems_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 306,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, I imagined to support the multi-host use-case the `xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Decorator.ManagedHost` interface would need to be searched. Those D-Bus objects would also have to have the `identifying` association to get/set the relevant LED.\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/bmcweb/blob/50d9f38ab85cef8b09c5968d7df3be948cf50d2f/redfish-core/lib/led.hpp#L285"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/systems_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 306,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "I've added the `xyz.openbmc_project.Inventory.Decorator.ManagedHost` interface here. Our systems do not have multi-host so it was not tested.\n\n@alexander.hansen@9elements.com: Any help here with testing this with multi-host system?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/systems_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 306,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't think it should require any testing specifically for multi-host.\n\nIf the `identifying` association is there, it should work the same as on your system since the same code path is used.\n\nThanks you for resolving this!"
                }
            ],
